          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#statement Statement
          %p
            A famous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            says (
            %a{:href => "#MinasianMoore97"}> Minasian-Moore 97
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten00"} Witten 00
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Moore02"} Moore 02
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Manjarin04"} Manjarín 04
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Evslin06"} Evslin 06
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Fredenhagen08"} Fredenhagen 08
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluxes"} fluxes
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} quantized
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theory
            known as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            and more generally in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR+cohomology+theory"} KR cohomology theory
            in the presence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"} type I string theory
            right on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-planes"} O-planes
          %p
            More generally, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluxes"} fluxes
            of the NS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            are jointly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} flux-quantized
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+topological+K-theory"} twisted topological K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            constituting the twist.
          %p
            Yet more generally, the conjecture says that, over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+K-theory"} orbifold K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            for the usual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+quotient+orbifolds"} global quotient orbifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant K-theory
            for the combined
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DistlerFreedMoore09"} Distler-Freed-Moore 09
          %p
            This means, or would mean, that the full massless
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} physical fields
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potentials"} gauge potentials
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in a
            = succeed "-version" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theories"} generalized cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            if the B-field is ignored, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+K-theory"} twisted differential K-theory
            if the B-field is included, and in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+differential+K-theory"} twisted equivariant differential K-theory
            if also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            are taken into account.
          %h3#motivation Motivation
          %p
            An immediate way to motivate the conjecture is to notice that the image of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Chern+character"} twisted Chern character
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            (say in degree 0, hence in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/TwistedChernCharacterAndRRFluxBianchi.jpg", :width => "800px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Twisted+Cohomotopy+implies+M5-brane+anomaly+cancellation"} SS20
          %p
            takes values in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted de Rham cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            are collections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            satisfying exactly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \, H_3 = 0
                  \\,,
                  \\;\;\;
                  d\, F_{2k + 2} = H_3 \wedge F_{2k}
          %p
            expected of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluxes"} fluxes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{2k}
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MinasianMoore97"} Minasian-Moore 97
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BrodzkiMathaiRosenbergSzabo06"} Brodzki-Mathai-Rosenberg-Szabo 06
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AntiBraneAnnihilationAsKGroupEquivRelation.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Stable+Cohomotopy+and+Branes"} Sch 18
          %p
            A conceptual picture of why
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            would capture
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            charge was suggested in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98, Section 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
            expected (this is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
            from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Sen's+conjecture#ReferencesForSuperstrings"} Sen 98
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            between
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-D-branes"} anti-D-branes
            plausibly implements on their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            (
            %a{:href => "topological+K-theory#eq:DefiningEquivalenceRelation"}> here
            ) of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %p
            While plausible and widely accepted in the string theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CheckingSenConjecture"} below
          %h2#OpenProblems Open problems
          %p
            While the conjecture that D-brane charge is in K-theory has become widely accepted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            in much of the
            = succeed "-community," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "-statements" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            = succeed "-physics," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of non-perturbative string theory (aka
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "M-theory#TheOpenProblem"} M-theory – the open problem
          %p Moreover, there are a number of indications that the conjecture can not actually be true without some modification, as in parts it seems to be in contradiction with other accepted facts about string theory. We list some of these issues in the following.
          %p
            Since the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            = succeed "-completion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is thought to involve not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            coupled to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "]," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+type+IIA+string+theory+and+M-theory"} duality between type IIA string theory and M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
            coupled to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BDHKMMS01"} BDHKMMS 01, Sec. 4.6.5
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge/flux quantization
            law, which would reduce to something close to K-theoretic charge quantization in the appropriate limit. See the last item
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LiftToMTheory"} below
          %h3#CheckingSenConjecture Checking Sen’s conjecture
          %p
            While the proposal of
            %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98, Section 3
            to explain the K-theory charge quantization conjecture via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstrings"} superstrings
            stretched between
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+D-brane"} anti D-brane
            pairs has become widely accepted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} open superstring tachyon condensation
            seems to be
            %a{:href => "#Erler13"} Erler 13
            which, however, concludes (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1308.4400.pdf#page=32"} p. 32
          %blockquote
            %p
              It would also be interesting to see if these developments can shed light on the long-speculated relation between string field theory and the K-theoretic description of D-brane charge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "D-brane#DBraneChargeQuantizationInTopologicalKTheory"} 75, 76, 77
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "#Erler19"} Erler 19
            which still lists this (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.00521.pdf#page=113"} p. 112
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %blockquote
            %p Are there topological invariants of the open string star algebra representing D-brane charges?
          %h3#incompatibility_with_sduality Incompatibility with S-duality
          %p
            Taken at face value, the K-theory conjecture applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            breaks the expected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            symmetry of the theory: Under this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "-flux" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            3-flux
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_3
            appear on the same footing and in particular mix as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            (jointly coupling to
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28p%2Cq%29-strings"} (p,q)-strings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            is part of the twist, while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_3
            is part of what is being twisted, with no evident way to mix these two concepts.
          %p
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Evslin06"} Evslin 06, Sec. 8.3
          %h3#spurious_fractional_dbrane_charges Spurious fractional D-brane charges
          %p
            An old argument of
            %a{:href => "#BDHKMMS01"} BDHKMMS 01, Sec. 4.5.2
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            by itself produces spurious
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-brane"} fractional D-brane
            charges that need to be eliminated by some modification of the K-theory conjecture.
          %p
            Evidence that this correction is provided by lifting to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+Cohomotopy"} equivariant stable Cohomotopy
            instead (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ) is offered in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Lift+of+fractional+D-brane+charge+to+equivariant+Cohomotopy+theory"} BSS 20
          %h3#spurious_dbrane_charges_on_group_manifolds Spurious D-brane charges on group manifolds
          %p
            Similarly, the analysis of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conformal+field+theory"} boundary conformal field theory
            describing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+models"}> WZW models
            ) does not seem to always agree with the conjectured K-theory classification of the corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
          %p
            %a{:href => "#FredenhagenQuella05"}> Fredenhagen-Quella 05
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p It might surprise that despite all the progress that has been made in understanding branes on group manifolds, there are usually not enough D-branes known to explain the whole charge group predicted by (twisted) K-theory.
          %h3#LiftToMTheory Lift to M-theory
          %p
            Finally, the lift of the putative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            has remained largely open and problematic, as maybe first highlighted in
            %a{:href => "#BDHKMMS01"} BDHKMMS 01, Sec. 4.6.5
            for a variety of reasons.
          %p
            However, a highly non-trivial check in
            %a{:href => "#DMW00"} DMW 00
            successfully matched the first non-trivial differential in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-fied
            flux
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            obtained from a
            = succeed "-argument" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
          %p
            Incidentally, this and related conditions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
            derived in
            %a{:href => "#DMW00"} DMW 00
            from a
            = succeed "-argument" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            are all implied also by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
            that the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantized
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy+theory"} twisted Cohomotopy theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Cohomotopy+implies+M-theory+anomaly+cancellation+on+8-manifolds"}> FSS 19
            ).
          %h3#UnstableKTheory Unstable K-theory?
          %p
            In view of potential lifts to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            discussed
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LiftToMTheory"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            (under the supposed
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            %em not at face value
            produce the high-degree RR-flux forms and their low-degree
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge duals
            – notably the RR 10-form and its dual 0-form (related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+brane"} exotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%28-2%29-branes"} D(-2)-branes
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber24"} Sati &amp; Schreiber 2024, Ex. 2.13
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+string+theory"} massive type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is at best subtle).
          %p
            But without these forms to complete the potential image of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            map for
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
          %p
            What could still work in this case is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantization
            in some unstable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            theory (for exposition see
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+flux+quantization"} geometry of physics – flux quantization
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+K-theory"} unstable K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern forms
            is bounded above.
          %p There are some further hints that make this plausible:
          %p
            As mentioned above,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
            motivates the equivalence relation that suggests classifying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+bundles"} Chan-Paton bundles
            of D-brane-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+D-brane"} antibrane
            systems in topological K-theory. In particular, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
            of such bundles is not restricted, which is argued to be required by the schematic construction of lower-dimensional D-branes as bound states of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D9-brane"} D9 brane-antibrane
            systems in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} IIB
          %p
            But in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Horava98"} Hořava 1998
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon"} unstable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D9+branes"} D9 branes
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^k
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            in the sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-branes
            from unstable D9-branes, then for that particular construction sixteen unstable D9-branes, i.e.
            = succeed "-bundles," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 16
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(16)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of D0-branes. The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\to\infty
            limit is argued to connect to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} Matrix theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+K-theory"} unstable K-theory
            may be a valid flux/charge quantization law.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#holographic_relation_to_topological_phases_of_matter Holographic relation to topological phases of matter
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality+in+solid+state+physics"} AdS/CFT duality in solid state physics
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
            (
            %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi10a"}> Ryu-Takayanagi 10a
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi10b"} Ryu-Takayanagi 10v
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#DBraneChargeQuantizationInTopologicalKTheory D-brane charge quantization in topological K-theory
            %p
              On the conjectural
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge+quantization+in+topological+K-theory"} D-brane charge quantization in topological K-theory
            %h4#origin_and_basics Origin and basics
            %p
              The idea that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              originates with the observation that their charge expressed in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
              resembles the image of a
              = succeed ":" do
